                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-phosphor/health/phosphor-health-monitor_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't know why we keep disabling this everywhere by default.  Once we get into production we should be re-enabling this check."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-phosphor/health/phosphor-health-monitor_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Fred Chen",
                        "email": "Fred.Chen@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "fredchenquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Checked with other projects \u2014 this was added because the BMC will reboot under stress or high load. Should we keep the reboot mechanism for now, or re-enabling it later when going into production?\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-phosphor/health/phosphor-health-monitor_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "We want the CPU_CRIT_TGT to be a valid value once we go into production.  We need to get a handle on what \"under stress or high load\" means because most of the time I've seen this is induced by some external test automation.  Having the BMC reboot when it's load is abnormally high is why phosphor-health-monitor exists, so we shouldn't be disabling that functionality."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-phosphor/health/phosphor-health-monitor_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Fred Chen",
                        "email": "Fred.Chen@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "fredchenquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Noted, I will re-enable it before production. Thanks\uff01"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-phosphor/health/phosphor-health-monitor_%.bbappend",
                    "line": 1,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Fred Chen",
                        "email": "Fred.Chen@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "fredchenquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-phosphor/images/fb-santabarbara-phosphor-image.inc",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "Do you need phosphor-gpio-monitor or phosphor-power-control for power-control?\nOr you need phosphor-gpio-monitor just to monitor the power good GPIOS?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meta-facebook/meta-santabarbara/recipes-phosphor/images/fb-santabarbara-phosphor-image.inc",
                    "line": 19,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Fred Chen",
                        "email": "Fred.Chen@quantatw.com",
                        "username": "fredchenquanta"
                    },
                    "message": "Currently, we\u2019re using phosphor-gpio-monitor just to log the power good GPIOs.\nFor power control, we plan to use phosphor-state-manager to handle it."
                },
